# The story comics (docs/plans/realm-ui.md, Phase 4): the comic viewer (StoryComic), laid out as
# intro-<realm>.jpg. story.play plays Campaign I's I-A over the home menu in Đại Long's look: its
# panel (the sequence, the panel and their count, the narration, the bubbles' speakers, texts and
# kinds, a flashback's sepia), the bar (the campaign line, the title, the dots, "Panel N of M",
# Back disabled on the first panel), stepping through it with Next, Back and the keys (Right,
# Space, Enter forward; Left back), Continue on the last panel, which ends it without touching the
# profile; seen=true records it once Skip ends it, and Escape skips too. The layout at 100%, 200% and
# 75% UI scale in each realm (ui.realm): the hidden test campaigns' sequences, a group bubble and
# bold ink, and a dynamic panel listing the player's stele lines. In a game, the simulation stays
# paused while a sequence plays. Then the campaign flow: Campaign I from Home plays I-A before its
# first briefing (paused, Back and the keys), Skip lands on the briefing and records it seen, the
# briefing's Replay the story plays it again over it (recording nothing), the layout with that
# button in each realm and scale, Campaign I's campaign-complete screen without Watch the epilogue,
# and neither starting the mission again nor loading a save of it plays I-A again. Each hidden test
# campaign plays its sequence before its first mission's briefing and, on the debrief's Continue,
# its sequence after it (over the debrief), then the world map, in its realm's look; a second start
# plays neither. test_choices' campaign-complete screen offers Watch the epilogue (each realm and
# scale), which plays over it, recording nothing (Return to the menu then records it without
# playing it again); unseen and not watched, Return to the menu plays it first.
# Last, Home's Replay the story (its subline; with Continue's subline Home still doesn't scroll,
# each realm and scale) plays the sequences seen in order: Continue goes on to the next, Skip ends
# it. Screenshots go to out/ui_story/.
#
# Run it with --fresh-profile, as CI does, at 1280 × 720, 1440 × 800 (CI's) and 1920 × 1080:
#   cargo run -p HeritageBuilder -- --fresh-profile --window-size 1440x800 --script crates/game/tests/scenarios/ui_story.jsonl
{"method": "time.fixed_dt", "params": {"dt": 0.016667}}
{"method": "input.move", "params": {"park": true}}
{"method": "wait.frames", "params": {"frames": 3}}
# Listing the widgets turns the widget registry on, for the ui.tree queries below.
{"method": "ui.tree", "params": {"filter": "Home/", "fields": ["path"]}}
{"method": "assert.eq", "params": {"query": "dialog.list", "path": "/dialogs/StoryComic", "value": false}}

